/A 922 0 R
/Alt (Panel A displays a schematic illustrating the process of isolating and culturing human periodontal ligament stem cells \(hPDLSCs\) from a tooth via dissection, digestion, and cell culture. Panel B shows a microscopic image of cultured hPDLSCs with a colony circled and a 200 micrometer scale bar. Panel C consists of six flow cytometry histograms demonstrating marker expression profiles, including high positivity for CD90, CD105, CD166, and CD44, and low positivity for CD34, CD45, and HLA-DR, with hPDLSCs indicated in pink and blank controls in blue. Panel D presents three microscopic images showing staining results for differentiated cell types, each with a 200 micrometer scale bar.)
